/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain PHP Session Management mechanics, detailing session_start\(\), cookie parameters, session fixation, and secure session destruction.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   HTTP is a stateless protocol. PHP uses Sessions to preserve user state across consecutive) Tj
T*
(   requests:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Session Mechanics:) Tj
T*
(   1. Initialization: Calling `session_start\(\)` checks for a session cookie \(`PHPSESSID`\). If) Tj
T*
(   missing, it generates a 128-bit random session identifier, sets a client cookie, and creates an) Tj
T*
(   associated state file on the server.) Tj
T*
(   2. Secure Cookie Configuration \(Must be set BEFORE session_start\(\)\):) Tj
T*
(   ```php) Tj
T*
(   session_set_cookie_params\([) Tj
T*
(   'lifetime' => 0, // Expire on browser close) Tj
T*
(   'path' => '/',) Tj
T*
(   'domain' => 'example.com',) Tj
T*
(   'secure' => true, // HTTPS only) Tj
T*
(   'httponly' => true, // Inaccessible to client JavaScript \(anti-XSS\)) Tj
T*
(   'samesite' => 'Strict' // Anti-CSRF defense) Tj
T*
(   ]\);) Tj
T*
(   session_start\(\);) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
