(   3. Session Fixation Defense:) Tj
T*
(   Whenever a user transitions from anonymous to authenticated, call `session_regenerate_id\(true\)`) Tj
T*
(   to destroy the old session ID and issue a new one.) Tj
T*
(   4. Complete Session Teardown \(Logout\):) Tj
T*
(   ```php) Tj
T*
(   $_SESSION = [];) Tj
T*
(   if \(ini_get\('session.use_cookies'\)\) {) Tj
T*
(   $params = session_get_cookie_params\(\);) Tj
T*
(   setcookie\(session_name\(\), '', time\(\) - 42000, $params['path'], $params['domain'],) Tj
T*
(   $params['secure'], $params['httponly']\);) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   session_destroy\(\);) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 5:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze SQL Injection \(SQLi\) attacks, demonstrating vulnerable code vs immune PDO Prepared Statements with Parameterized Queries.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   SQL Injection occurs when untrusted input alters the syntactic structure of an executed SQL) Tj
T*
(   command:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Vulnerable Dynamic Concatenation:) Tj
T*
(   ```php) Tj
T*
(   // FATAL VULNERABILITY:) Tj
T*
(   $user = $_POST['username'];) Tj
T*
(   $sql = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = '$user'";) Tj
T*
(   // Attacker inputs: ' OR '1'='1) Tj
T*
(   // Resulting query: SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = '' OR '1'='1') Tj
T*
(   // Dumps the entire user database!) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Infallible Defense: PDO Prepared Statements:) Tj
T*
(   ```php) Tj
T*
(   $stmt = $pdo->prepare\('SELECT id, email, role FROM users WHERE username = :user AND status =) Tj
T*
(   :status'\);) Tj
T*
(   // Parameterized execution:) Tj
T*
(   $stmt->execute\([) Tj
T*
(   'user' => $_POST['username'],) Tj
T*
(   'status' => 'active') Tj
T*
(   ]\);) Tj
T*
(   $results = $stmt->fetchAll\(PDO::FETCH_ASSOC\);) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
(   Why It Guarantees Immunity:) Tj
T*
(   The database engine pre-compiles the SQL syntax into an execution plan. The bound parameters) Tj
T*
(   are transmitted independently as raw data literals. Even if the parameter contains `' OR) Tj
T*
(   '1'='1; DROP TABLE users;`, the database treats it strictly as a literal username string,) Tj
T*
(   completely neutralizing SQL injection.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
