(   Cross-Site Scripting allows attackers to execute malicious JavaScript in victims' browsers,) Tj
T*
(   hijacking sessions or defacing pages:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Server-Side Defensive Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   1. HTML Entity Encoding via `htmlspecialchars\(\)`:) Tj
T*
(   Before outputting any user-supplied variable into HTML context, convert special characters into) Tj
T*
(   safe HTML entities:) Tj
T*
(   ```php) Tj
T*
(   echo '<p>Welcome, ' . htmlspecialchars\($userInput, ENT_QUOTES | ENT_HTML5, 'UTF-8'\) . '</p>';) Tj
T*
(   // Converts <script> into &lt;script&gt; rendering text visibly without execution) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Context-Aware Escaping Rules:) Tj
T*
(   - Inside HTML Body: Use `htmlspecialchars\(\)`.) Tj
T*
(   - Inside HTML Attributes \(`<input value="...">`\): Ensure attribute values are enclosed in) Tj
T*
(   quotes and encoded with `ENT_QUOTES`.) Tj
T*
(   - Inside JavaScript Context \(`<script>var data = ...;</script>`\): Encode via) Tj
T*
(   `json_encode\($data, JSON_HEX_TAG | JSON_HEX_AMP | JSON_HEX_APOS | JSON_HEX_QUOT\)`.) Tj
T*
(   - Inside URLs: Use `urlencode\(\)` and whitelist protocols \(rejecting `javascript:`) Tj
T*
(   pseudoprotocols\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Defense-in-Depth: Enforce Content Security Policy \(CSP\) headers to block unauthorized script) Tj
T*
(   execution.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
