(>> Solution to Question 7:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Cross-Site Request Forgery \(CSRF\) defense using Anti-CSRF Synchronizer Tokens and SameSite cookies.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   CSRF tricks an authenticated user's browser into submitting unauthorized transactions to a web) Tj
T*
(   application:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The Synchronizer Token Pattern Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   1. Token Generation upon Session Creation:) Tj
T*
(   ```php) Tj
T*
(   if \(empty\($_SESSION['csrf_token']\)\) {) Tj
T*
(   $_SESSION['csrf_token'] = bin2hex\(random_bytes\(32\)\); // 64-character cryptographic token) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Injection into Form HTML:) Tj
T*
(   ```html) Tj
T*
(   <form action="/transfer.php" method="POST">) Tj
T*
(   <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="<?= htmlspecialchars\($_SESSION['csrf_token']\)) Tj
T*
(   ?>">) Tj
T*
(   <input type="number" name="amount">) Tj
T*
(   <button type="submit">Send Funds</button>) Tj
T*
(   </form>) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Verification on POST Handler:) Tj
T*
(   ```php) Tj
T*
(   if \($_SERVER['REQUEST_METHOD'] === 'POST'\) {) Tj
T*
(   if \(!isset\($_POST['csrf_token']\) || !hash_equals\($_SESSION['csrf_token'],) Tj
T*
ET

