(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the architecture of XML technologies: XML syntax rules, Document Type Definitions \(DTD\), and XML Schema \(XSD\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   XML is a self-describing, structured data interchange format designed for cross-platform data) Tj
T*
(   exchange:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. XML Syntax Rules \(Well-Formedness\):) Tj
T*
(   - Must have exactly one root element enclosing all other nodes.) Tj
T*
(   - All tags must be strictly closed \(`<tag></tag>` or `<tag/>`\).) Tj
T*
(   - XML is strictly case-sensitive \(`<Price>` != `<price>`\).) Tj
T*
(   - Attribute values must always be quoted \(`id="101"`\).) Tj
T*
(   - Reserved characters must use predefined entities \(`&lt;`, `&gt;`, `&amp;`, `&apos;`,) Tj
T*
(   `&quot;`\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. DTD \(Document Type Definition\):) Tj
T*
(   Specifies element structure using SGML-based syntax \(`<!ELEMENT book \(title, author, price\)>`\).) Tj
T*
(   Lacks data type constraints \(treats all values as character text\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. XML Schema Definition \(XSD\):) Tj
T*
(   Modern W3C standard written in XML syntax itself \(`<xs:schema>`\). Supports strong data typing) Tj
T*
(   \(`xs:integer`, `xs:date`, `xs:decimal`\), regex restrictions, min/max occurrences, and) Tj
T*
(   namespaces, making it standard for enterprise systems.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
