(   [Problem Statement]: Compare SOAP and RESTful Web Services across protocol layers, data formats, statefulness, performance, and tooling.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   SOAP and REST represent two foundational distributed computing paradigms:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. SOAP \(Simple Object Access Protocol\):) Tj
T*
(   - Nature: Strict, standardized protocol defined by W3C specification.) Tj
T*
(   - Data Format: Strictly XML-only wrapped in standardized SOAP Envelopes.) Tj
T*
(   - Contract: Formal WSDL contract defining data structures and operations.) Tj
T*
(   - Transport: Operates over HTTP, SMTP, TCP, or JMS.) Tj
T*
(   - Security: WS-Security standard providing enterprise-grade, message-level end-to-end) Tj
T*
(   encryption.) Tj
T*
(   - Overhead: Heavyweight XML parsing overhead; high bandwidth consumption.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. REST \(Representational State Transfer\):) Tj
T*
(   - Nature: Lightweight architectural style leveraging native HTTP mechanisms.) Tj
T*
(   - Data Format: Flexible \(JSON, XML, YAML, HTML\); predominantly JSON.) Tj
T*
(   - Contract: Informal or OpenAPI / Swagger specifications.) Tj
T*
(   - Transport: Strictly HTTP/HTTPS using standard verbs \(GET, POST, PUT, DELETE\).) Tj
T*
(   - Security: Relies on HTTPS/TLS and token-based authentication \(OAuth 2.0 / JWT\).) Tj
T*
(   - Performance: Fast, lightweight, cacheable, and mobile-friendly.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 11:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain RESTful API Architectural Constraints: Statelessness, Client-Server, Cacheability, Uniform Interface, and Layered System.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Roy Fielding defined six architectural constraints that characterize a true RESTful web) Tj
T*
(   service:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Client-Server: Separation of user interface concerns \(client\) from data storage and business) Tj
T*
(   logic \(server\), allowing independent evolution.) Tj
T*
(   2. Statelessness: Each request from client to server must contain ALL information necessary to) Tj
T*
(   understand and process the request. No client context is stored on the server between requests) Tj
T*
(   \(enables effortless horizontal scaling across server farms\).) Tj
T*
ET

