(   3. Cacheability: Responses must explicitly define themselves as cacheable or non-cacheable \(via) Tj
T*
(   `Cache-Control` headers\) to prevent stale data while eliminating redundant server hits.) Tj
T*
(   4. Uniform Interface: Standardized interaction contract across four tenets: identification of) Tj
T*
(   resources \(URIs\), manipulation through representations \(JSON\), self-descriptive messages, and) Tj
T*
(   HATEOAS.) Tj
T*
(   5. Layered System: The client cannot tell whether it is connected directly to the end server or) Tj
T*
(   an intermediate proxy, CDN, or load balancer.) Tj
T*
(   6. Code on Demand \(Optional\): Server temporarily extends client functionality by transferring) Tj
T*
