(   [Problem Statement]: Explain JSON Web Tokens \(JWT\) architecture, detailing Header, Payload \(Claims\), Signature generation, and verification workflow.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   JSON Web Tokens \(RFC 7519\) provide an open, compact, self-contained mechanism for securely) Tj
T*
(   transmitting authenticated claims between parties:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Anatomy of a JWT String \(Header.Payload.Signature\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Header: JSON specifying token type and signing algorithm: `{"alg": "HS256", "typ": "JWT"}`) Tj
T*
(   \(Base64URL encoded\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Payload: JSON containing Claims \(statements about an entity and metadata\):) Tj
T*
(   - Registered Claims: `iss` \(issuer\), `exp` \(expiration timestamp\), `sub` \(subject user ID\),) Tj
T*
(   `iat` \(issued at\).) Tj
T*
(   - Custom Claims: `{"userId": 4821, "role": "admin"}`.) Tj
T*
(   - Encoded as Base64URL \(NOT encrypted! Anyone can decode and inspect claims\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Signature:) Tj
T*
(   Generated by taking the encoded header, encoded payload, secret key, and algorithm:) Tj
T*
(   `Signature = HMACSHA256\(base64UrlEncode\(header\) + "." + base64UrlEncode\(payload\), secretKey\)`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Verification Workflow:) Tj
T*
(   When client sends `Authorization: Bearer <token>`, the backend server splits the string,) Tj
T*
(   independently hashes `header + "." + payload` with its secret key, and compares it to the) Tj
T*
(   incoming Signature using `hash_equals\(\)`. If matched, the claims are authentic and untampered.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
