(   [Problem Statement]: Explain XML External Entity \(XXE\) injection vulnerabilities and detail how to configure XML parsers to disable entity resolution.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   XXE injection targets weakly configured XML parsers processing XML inputs containing malicious) Tj
T*
(   Document Type Definitions \(DTDs\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Attack Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   ```xml) Tj
T*
(   <?xml version="1.0" encoding="ISO-8859-1"?>) Tj
T*
(   <!DOCTYPE foo [) Tj
T*
(   <!ELEMENT foo ANY >) Tj
T*
(   <!ENTITY xxe SYSTEM "file:///etc/passwd" >]>) Tj
T*
(   <user>) Tj
T*
(   <username>&xxe;</username>) Tj
T*
(   </user>) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
(   When the server parses `&xxe;`, the XML parser reads the server's local `/etc/passwd` file and) Tj
T*
(   embeds its contents in the parsed username object!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Defense in PHP:) Tj
T*
(   Explicitly disable external entity loading before parsing:) Tj
T*
(   ```php) Tj
T*
(   libxml_disable_entity_loader\(true\); // Disables external entities) Tj
T*
(   $dom = new DOMDocument\(\);) Tj
T*
(   $dom->loadXML\($xmlString, LIBXML_NOENT | LIBXML_DTDLOAD\); // Safe loading) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
