(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Two-Factor Authentication \(2FA\) implementation in web applications using Time-Based One-Time Password \(TOTP\) algorithm \(RFC 6238\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   TOTP generates rotating 6-digit verification codes shared between server and mobile) Tj
T*
(   authenticator app \(Google Authenticator\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Algorithm Mechanics:) Tj
T*
(   1. Shared Secret: Upon setup, server generates a random base32 secret key, displayed to user as) Tj
T*
(   a QR code \(`otpauth://totp/App:User?secret=JBSWY3DPEHPK3PXP`\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Time Counter: Both phone and server compute the current time step counter: `T =) Tj
T*
(   floor\(UnixTime / 30 seconds\)`.) Tj
T*
(   3. HMAC Hash: Both compute `HMAC-SHA1\(SecretKey, T\)`.) Tj
T*
(   4. Dynamic Truncation: The hash bytes are truncated to extract a 6-digit integer.) Tj
T*
(   5. Verification: When user inputs their 6-digit code, the server computes the expected code for) Tj
T*
(   time windows `T`, `T-1`, and `T+1` \(allowing for slight clock drift\). If match occurs,) Tj
T*
(   authentication succeeds.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
