(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze Web Application security auditing tools: OWASP ZAP, Burp Suite, SQLMap, and Nikto in penetration testing workflows.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Security assurance mandates regular automated and manual penetration testing:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Security Tool Profiles:) Tj
T*
(   1. Burp Suite: The industry-standard intercepting proxy for manual web application testing.) Tj
T*
(   Intercepts, inspects, and tampers with HTTP/S requests and responses in flight \(Repeater,) Tj
T*
(   Intruder, Scanner\).) Tj
T*
(   2. OWASP ZAP \(Zed Attack Proxy\): Open-source automated vulnerability scanner for detecting) Tj
T*
(   OWASP Top 10 flaws \(XSS, CSRF, insecure headers, SQLi\) in CI/CD build pipelines.) Tj
T*
(   3. SQLMap: Advanced automated penetration testing tool that detects and exploits SQL injection) Tj
T*
(   flaws, automating database fingerprinting, schema dumping, and data extraction.) Tj
T*
(   4. Nikto: Command-line web server scanner that tests for dangerous server misconfigurations,) Tj
T*
(   outdated software versions, and default files across 6,700+ vulnerability signatures.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
